Station: Bori-police-station, Bori Metropolis.

The interpreted subsurface consists of four layers with resistivities of 150 $\Omega$m (1.23m), 97.1 $\Omega$m (6.21m), 284 $\Omega$m (37.5m), and 700 $\Omega$m. Based on the resistivity sequence, the first group of three layers (150-97.1-284) follows an H-type pattern ($r_1 > r_2 < r_3$), and the second group (97.1-284-700) follows an A-type pattern ($r_1 < r_2 < r_3$). This results in an HA curve type. Please note that the on-file classification of HK-type is incorrect, as the final resistivity increase does not match the K-type requirement ($r_2 < r_3 > r_4$).

